# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Dependencies
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
package-lock.json.bak

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Live database — REAL USER DATA. Never commit.
#
# Contains user accounts, password hashes, the Club Credit ledger, chat
# messages and session records. Note that SQLite's write-ahead log and shared
# memory files hold committed AND uncommitted rows and are frequently LARGER
# than the .sqlite file itself — excluding only the main database is not
# enough, which is why every sidecar extension is listed explicitly.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
app/data/
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm
*.sqlite3
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.db-journal

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# User-uploaded content — real files uploaded by real people.
# The directory structure is kept (via .gitkeep) so a fresh clone still runs.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
app/public/uploads/*
!app/public/uploads/.gitkeep
!app/public/uploads/*/
app/public/uploads/**/*
!app/public/uploads/**/.gitkeep

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated / build output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
site/dist/
site/out/
logs/
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor / OS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Database, second pass — unanchored, following the file type not the folder.
#
# server/db.js makes the database location env-overridable
# (WGC_DB_PATH || app/data/winners.sqlite), so the file can legitimately be
# created somewhere the path-anchored `app/data/` rule above would never see.
# These rules hold wherever it lands.
#
# The globs deliberately run PAST the extension: SQLite names its sidecars by
# appending to the whole filename, so a WGC_DB_PATH of `wgc.sqlite3` yields
# `wgc.sqlite3-wal` / `wgc.sqlite3-shm`, which `*.sqlite-wal` above does not
# match — and a WAL fallback on a `.sqlite` file yields `-journal`, which
# `*.db-journal` does not match either. One trailing `*` covers every present
# and future sidecar suffix in each family at once.
#
# `data/` is unanchored on purpose: `app/data/` above only protects that one
# directory, and a database given a path with no recognisable extension (e.g.
# WGC_DB_PATH=./data/wgc) would otherwise be caught by nothing at all.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.sqlite*
*.db-*
data/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# User-uploaded content, second pass — unanchored, and directory-safe.
#
# This restates the app/public/uploads/ block above rather than trusting it,
# for two reasons:
#
#  1. It follows the `uploads` NAME rather than one hardcoded path, so the
#     rule survives the upload directory being moved out of public/ (and any
#     later move) instead of silently going quiet at the moment it matters.
#  2. The block above ends up excluding the `chat/` directory ITSELF, and git
#     never descends into an excluded directory — so its `!.../**/.gitkeep`
#     negation can never fire, and the .gitkeep meant to preserve the
#     directory structure is unreachable. Re-including the DIRECTORIES (the
#     trailing slash restricts that negation to directories and never files)
#     lets git walk back in, leaves every actual upload ignored, and lets the
#     .gitkeep through so a fresh clone still has somewhere to write.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
**/uploads/**
!**/uploads/**/
!**/.gitkeep

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets — shapes the `.env` / `.env.*` rules above don't reach. Neither a
# direnv script nor a `<name>.env` file matches `.env.*`, which requires a
# literal dot straight after "env". `.env.example` is unaffected: it ends in
# `.example`, so `*.env` never matches it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.envrc
*.env

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Rotated logs — `*.log` above misses `app.log.1`, `pnpm-debug.log.2`, etc.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log.*
